      "math_academy_id": "e-12463",
      "problem": "The marginal mass functions of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(4,2).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f_X(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f_Y(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.55$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>",
